//RS /// D-CONC-SPAWN1=D (`Docs/spec/spec.md:2545`, `Docs/spec/syntax-decisions.md:2264`,
//RS /// `Syntax::KW_CONC_TASK`): `task` is the ONE reserved concurrency word, so a
//RS /// name position holding it is refused where it is written. That is a stronger
//RS /// form of this test's property than "it binds a list": the word can never be
//RS /// quietly read as a spawn, and it can never be quietly read as an ordinary
//RS /// name either. The earlier assertion (that the binding runs and prints 7)
//RS /// predates the reservation.
